    "created_at": "2025-02-27T15:17:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-27T15:17:42Z",
    "body": "Hi, I believe the Central device can start a connection parameter update. See the specification bellow:\n\nBLUETOOTH CORE SPECIFICATION Version 5.1 | Vol 6, Part B - 5.1.1  Connection Update procedure\n\nIf the master, the slave, or both do not support the Connection Parameters\n\nRequest Procedure, then the master shall send an\n\nLL_CONNECTION_UPDATE_IND PDU (the slave shall not send this PDU)\n\nwhile the slave shall use the L2CAP LE Signaling channel (see [Vol 3] Part A,\n\nSection 4.20 and Section 4.21).\n\nIf a device supports the Connection Parameters Request Procedure but does\n\nnot know whether its peer does (because neither device has previously\n\nattempted that procedure or performed a Feature Exchange Procedure), then it\n\nshall initiate the Connection Parameters Request Procedure and, if the peer\n\nresponds with an LL_UNKNOWN_RSP PDU, by then using the method\n\ndescribed in the previous  paragraph.\n\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
